irginia, and Rhode Island; distribution and sale of natural gas in Kentucky and Rhode Island; sale of wholesale electricity in Kentucky; and generation of electricity from power plants in Kentucky. It generates electricity from coal, gas, hydro, and solar sources. The company was formerly known as PP&L Resources, Inc. and changed its name to PPL Corporation in 2000. PPL Corporation was founded in 1920 and is headquartered in Allentown, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Vincent  Sorgi CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["PPL Corporation is a large-cap utilities business with a $26.9B market cap on $9.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $1.4B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 42% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.41707630505314247},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What PPL (PPL)'s Earnings Beat Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-ppl/ppl/news/what-ppl-ppls-earnings-beat-means-for-shareholders","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794617330.262,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PPL Stock Trading at a Premium to the Industry at 16.83X: How to Play?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029707/ppl-stock-trading-at-a-premium-to-the-industry-at-16-83x-how-to-play?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cmost_popular_stocks-3029707","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794584880.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Jefferies Financial Group Inc. Sells 940,581 Shares of PPL Corporation 